<title>THAILAND: Thai PM says no baht devaluation, Amnuay stays.</title>
<headline>Thai PM says no baht devaluation, Amnuay stays.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai prime minister's office said on Thursday that there was no reason to devalue the embattled baht and stressed that Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan would remain at his post.</p>
<p>&quot;The Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchiyudh confirmed today that there shall not be a reshuffle of the economic team headed by Amnuay Viravan, deputy prime minister and minister of finance,&quot; said a statement issued by the office.</p>
</text>
